          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong rectangular band
            or
            %strong nowhere commutative semigroup
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semigroup"} semigroup
            which satisfies any of these equivalent conditions
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                it is
                %em nowhere commutative
                in the sense that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                      %mo =
                      %mi b
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a b = b a
                implies that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo =
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a = b
                for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                      %mi a
                      %mo =
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a b a = a
                for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi a
                      %mi a
                      %mo =
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a a a = a
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                      %mo =
                      %mi a
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a b c = a c
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
          %p
            However, despite its name, there exist
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+semigroup"} commutative
            nowhere commutative semigroups, such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty
            semigroup and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+group"} trivial group
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A rectangular band is indeed a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/band"} band
                since the defining identity implies
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi y
                      %mi z
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y z = x z
                for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y,z
                whence by taking
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo =
                      %mi z
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y=z=x
                one gets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi x
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x x x = x x
                and from the defining identity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi x
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x x x=x
                hence
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mi x
                        %mo =
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x x = x
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi y
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y z
                by substituting
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi z
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x z x
                for
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi y
                      %mi z
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mi z
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi y
                      %mi z
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi xy
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mi z
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y z = (x z x) y z = x (z (xy) z) = x z \; .
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                is a rectangular band, then there exist
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} non-empty sets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
                as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semigroup"} semigroup
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo ×
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I\times J
                equipped with the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplication"} multiplication
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i, j)(p,q) = (i,q)
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i,p\in I
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j,q\in J
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/band"} band
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                has a decomposition as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi L
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_{x\in L} R_x
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                is a semilattice, each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_x
                is a
                = succeed "-semigroup" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} sub
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi y
                      %mo ⊆
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_x R_y \subseteq R_{x y}
                for every
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                from the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                of rectangular bands, because we lack connecting morphisms
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mi x
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_x \to R_y
          %h2#the_category_of_rectangular_bands The category of rectangular bands
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Rect
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rect
            be the category of rectangular bands with semigroup homomorphisms as morphisms.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Since rectangular bands are an equationally defined subclass of the class of all semigroups,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Rect
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rect
                is a subvariety of the variety
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SGr
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SGr
                of semigroups and hence enjoys all the usual (co)completeness properties of a variety.
            %li
              %p
                Since
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Rect
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rect
                is the 2-valued
                %span.newWikiWord
                  collapse
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/collapsed+topos"} ?
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set\times Set
                it is even a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
                variety. Since the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+law"} distributive law
                holds for (finite) coproducts in cartesian closed categories,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Rect
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rect
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+category"} distributive category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+category"} locally cartesian closed
                it is neither a topos nor even an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} extensive category
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#Johnstone90"} 1990
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semigroup"} semigroup
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/band"} band
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semilattice"} semilattice
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+category"} distributive category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reader+monad"} reader monad
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graphic+category"} graphic monoid
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord
                  collapsed topos
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/collapsed+topos"} ?
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Howie76
              %p
                J. Howie,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An introduction to semigroup theory
            %li#Johnstone90
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                ,
                %em Collapsed toposes and cartesian closed varieties
                , JPAA
                %strong 129
                (1990) pp.446-480.
            %li
              %p
                N. Kimura,
                %em The structure of idempotent semigroups I
                , Pacific Journal of Mathematics
                %strong 8
                no.2 (1958) pp.257-275. (
                %a{:href => "http://msp.org/pjm/1958/8-2/pjm-v8-n2-p07-p.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nowhere_commutative_semigroup"} Nowhere commutative semigroup
